       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day in many references), so this is about 5 times the maximum. A single 4,250 mg dose is also well above anything given at once, and doses at that level risk severe lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **425 mg PO TID**, which isn't a standard tablet strength but would be a low dose\n- **1,000 mg PO BID** (2,000 mg/day)\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg PO daily or BID with meals, titrated up\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 4,250 mg really is what you intend, please confirm that. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
